Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions.id` : question identifier – will appear in the result set.  
• `…posts_questions.title` : search for the word “how” and for exclusion words.  
• `…posts_questions.body` : same filtering as `title`.  
• `…posts_questions.tags` : check whether the question is tagged with one of the Android tags (`LIKE '%<android‑layout>%`', etc.).  
• `…posts_questions.view_count` : used to rank (highest views first) and pick the “top 50”.  
• `…posts_questions.creation_date` (optional) : may be selected just for extra information, but is not required.  

Filtering conditions that will repeatedly appear  

```text
1)   (REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(title) ,  r'\bhow\b')
     OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(body) , r'\bhow\b'))

2)   NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(title), r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
     AND
     NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(body) , r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
```

Below are ten different BigQuery queries (each capped with `LIMIT 20`) that gradually move from simple exploration to the final solution.

```sql
-- 1) Quick look at questions that contain the tag <android-layout>
SELECT id, title, view_count, tags
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE tags LIKE '%<android-layout>%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Same tag, but the title OR body must contain the word "how"
SELECT id, title, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE tags LIKE '%<android-layout>%'
  AND (REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(title), r'\bhow\b')
       OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(body) , r'\bhow\b'))
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Add the “no‑troubleshooting” exclusion list
SELECT id, title, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE tags LIKE '%<android-layout>%'
  AND (REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(title), r'\bhow\b')
       OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(body) , r'\bhow\b'))
  AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(title), r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
  AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(body) , r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Apply the same criteria to a different tag: <android-activity>
SELECT id, title, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE tags LIKE '%<android-activity>%'
  AND (REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(title), r'\bhow\b')
       OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(body) , r'\bhow\b'))
  AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(title), r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
  AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(body) , r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Count how many qualifying questions exist for every tag in our list
WITH tag_list AS (
  SELECT 'android-layout'  AS tag UNION ALL SELECT 'android-activity'  UNION ALL
  SELECT 'android-intent'  UNION ALL SELECT 'android-edittext'  UNION ALL
  SELECT 'android-fragments' UNION ALL SELECT 'android-recyclerview' UNION ALL
  SELECT 'listview' UNION ALL SELECT 'android-actionbar' UNION ALL
  SELECT 'google-maps' UNION ALL SELECT 'android-asynctask'
)
SELECT tl.tag,
       COUNT(*) AS qualifying_questions
FROM tag_list AS tl
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
  ON q.tags LIKE CONCAT('%<', tl.tag,'>%')
WHERE (REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.title), r'\bhow\b')
       OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.body) , r'\bhow\b'))
  AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.title), r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
  AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.body) , r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
GROUP BY tl.tag
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Show the 20 most viewed “android-intent” questions that meet all rules
SELECT id, title, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE tags LIKE '%<android-intent>%'
  AND (REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(title), r'\bhow\b')
       OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(body) , r'\bhow\b'))
  AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(title), r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
  AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(body) , r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
ORDER BY view_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Same as (6) but using word‑boundary REGEX on the tag string itself
SELECT id, title, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags, r'(?i)<android-recyclerview>')
  AND (REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(title), r'\bhow\b')
       OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(body) , r'\bhow\b'))
  AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(title), r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
  AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(body) , r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
ORDER BY view_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Produce (for inspection) the top‑viewed question per tag
WITH tag_list AS (
  SELECT 'android-layout'  AS tag UNION ALL SELECT 'android-activity'  UNION ALL
  SELECT 'android-intent'  UNION ALL SELECT 'android-edittext'  UNION ALL
  SELECT 'android-fragments' UNION ALL SELECT 'android-recyclerview' UNION ALL
  SELECT 'listview' UNION ALL SELECT 'android-actionbar' UNION ALL
  SELECT 'google-maps' UNION ALL SELECT 'android-asynctask'
),
qualified AS (
  SELECT tl.tag,
         q.id,
         q.title,
         q.view_count,
         ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY tl.tag ORDER BY q.view_count DESC) AS rn
  FROM tag_list AS tl
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
    ON q.tags LIKE CONCAT('%<', tl.tag,'>%')
  WHERE (REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.title), r'\bhow\b')
         OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.body) , r'\bhow\b'))
    AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.title), r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
    AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.body) , r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
)
SELECT tag, id, title, view_count
FROM qualified
WHERE rn = 1                -- only the single most‑viewed question per tag
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same CTE as (8) but keep tags that have >= 50 qualified questions
WITH tag_list AS (
  SELECT 'android-layout'  AS tag UNION ALL SELECT 'android-activity'  UNION ALL
  SELECT 'android-intent'  UNION ALL SELECT 'android-edittext'  UNION ALL
  SELECT 'android-fragments' UNION ALL SELECT 'android-recyclerview' UNION ALL
  SELECT 'listview' UNION ALL SELECT 'android-actionbar' UNION ALL
  SELECT 'google-maps' UNION ALL SELECT 'android-asynctask'
),
qualified AS (
  SELECT tl.tag,
         q.id,
         q.title,
         q.view_count,
         ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY tl.tag ORDER BY q.view_count DESC) AS rn,
         COUNT(*)     OVER (PARTITION BY tl.tag) AS tag_total
  FROM tag_list AS tl
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
    ON q.tags LIKE CONCAT('%<', tl.tag,'>%')
  WHERE (REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.title), r'\bhow\b')
         OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.body) , r'\bhow\b'))
    AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.title), r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
    AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.body) , r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
)
SELECT tag, tag_total
FROM qualified
GROUP BY tag, tag_total
HAVING tag_total >= 50
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Final query – top 50 most‑viewed questions for every tag
--      that has at least 50 qualifying questions
WITH tag_list AS (
  SELECT 'android-layout'  AS tag UNION ALL SELECT 'android-activity'  UNION ALL
  SELECT 'android-intent'  UNION ALL SELECT 'android-edittext'  UNION ALL
  SELECT 'android-fragments' UNION ALL SELECT 'android-recyclerview' UNION ALL
  SELECT 'listview' UNION ALL SELECT 'android-actionbar' UNION ALL
  SELECT 'google-maps' UNION ALL SELECT 'android-asynctask'
),
qualified AS (
  SELECT tl.tag,
         q.id,
         q.title,
         q.view_count,
         ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY tl.tag ORDER BY q.view_count DESC)           AS rn,
         COUNT(*)     OVER (PARTITION BY tl.tag)                                      AS tag_total
  FROM tag_list AS tl
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
       ON q.tags LIKE CONCAT('%<', tl.tag,'>%')
  WHERE (REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.title), r'\bhow\b')
         OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.body) , r'\bhow\b'))
    AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.title), r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
    AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(q.body) , r'\b(fail|problem|error|wrong|fix|bug|issue|solve|trouble)\b')
)
SELECT tag,
       id,
       title,
       view_count
FROM qualified
WHERE tag_total >= 50   -- keep only sufficiently large tags
  AND rn <= 50          -- top 50 by view count within each tag
LIMIT 20;               -- sample 20 rows of the final data set
```

Each query is self‑contained, uses only the allowed tables, encloses identifiers with back‑ticks, and finishes with `LIMIT 20` as requested.
